Laurel corpus
=============

THE TEXTS
---------
The poems are in the public domain in the United States: all were published before 1931.
Nothing in this repository creates, asserts or implies any claim over them. They were taken
from Project Gutenberg; each work's TEI file names the ebook it came from and links to it.
The Gutenberg header, footer and licence text were removed; the verse itself was not altered.

THE APPARATUS
-------------
Everything Laurel added is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0). That covers:

  - the per-line scansion (@met and @real)
  - the rhyme lettering
  - the metre determinations and their confidence values
  - the canonical references and the permanent identifier registry
  - the line-level audio timings
  - the TEI encoding itself, and the selection and arrangement of the corpus

You may copy, redistribute, adapt and build upon this material, including commercially,
provided that you give appropriate credit to Laurel (laurelpoetry.com) and license your
contributions under the same terms.

Full licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

THE RECORDINGS
--------------
No audio is contained here, only timings. The recordings themselves are LibriVox readings,
dedicated to the public domain by their readers and hosted by the Internet Archive. Each
timing file names the reader and the LibriVox project the recording belongs to.
